  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DB7">Exercise <span data-tag="0DB7">111.44.4</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a projective surface over an algebraically closed field $k$. Show that for every $n \geq 0$ there exists a proper closed subscheme $Z \subset X$ such that $\dim _ k H^1(Z, \mathcal{O}_ Z) > n$. Only explain how to do this by modifying the arguments in Exercise <a href="/tag/0DB6" data-tag="0DB6">111.44.3</a> and <a href="/tag/0DB5" data-tag="0DB5">111.44.2</a>; don't give all the details. </p>
